  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to adjust probabilities below 20% by adding 10 percentage points and then compare the weighted sums. However, in this decision problem, no outcome has a probability below 20%, so no adjustment is made. The reason effectively reduces to comparing expected values. The individual did not mention any calculation of expected values or any adjustment of probabilities. Their justification was based on a qualitative comparison of the higher payoff in A and the higher probability in B, without any reference to weighting or adjusting probabilities. Since the individual did not consider the specific rule involving probability adjustments (even though it would not have changed the outcome here), and since they did not mention any weighted sum or expected value computation, there is no evidence that they applied the reason. The deliberation process does not align with the rule of the reason. Therefore, the reason was not used.",
